{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3058","id":4556135629,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABD5EczQ","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3058","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3058.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3058.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3058","number":3058,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Show captured output when backend dispatch assertions fail","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, degraded-unresolved, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nInclude captured guest stderr and stdout when the LiteInst, DBT, or KVM dispatch test fails its exit-status assertion. This makes the failure explain the launch at its own test site. The status and all subsequent output checks remain unchanged.\n\nThe original diagnostic was replayed on current main. The repeated historical comment was corrected following review: the DBT error was already present in a sibling test's log. This change makes it visible at the capturing test's failed assertion.\n\n## Determinism\n\nThe three status operands, guest commands, feature and availability checks, and following assertions are unchanged. Rust evaluates the new diagnostic formatting only after the status comparison fails, so successful test execution follows the same path.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nThis changes test failure messages. It does not change backend dispatch, syscall handling, captured bytes, or guest behavior. Lossy UTF-8 conversion is confined to the panic message; stdout and stderr assertions continue to compare the original bytes.\n\n## Validation\n\nAt ae27d95054e7a77bb6a9fea918fca90e812e3deb, the complete one-file diff and three assertion contexts were reviewed, Rust 2024 formatting, repository-selected cargo fmt --all -- --check, and git diff --check passed, and normal commit hooks passed. Removing the three diagnostic blocks reproduces the entire parent source byte-for-byte. No backend guest was rerun for this diagnostic change; it establishes no new determinism, parity, or main-green result.\n\nTask: liteinst-lane-to-full-determinism-and-parity. This lane is finishing the existing PR under the owner's queue-drain directive; the original author and earlier review remain credited in the retained history and commit body.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T08:03:13Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T14:14:04Z","closed_at":"2026-09-17T14:14:01Z","merged_at":"2026-09-17T14:14:00Z","merge_commit_sha":"421e08cefb8a6dd84ffc0fcf4a7bcbf5f64803bd","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3058/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3058/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3058/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/